# ============================================================
# BandIt — .dockerignore (whitelist style)
# ============================================================
# Deny everything, then allow back ONLY what the Dockerfile
# COPYs. Anything new that appears in the repo (a venv, a
# dataset, a checkpoint, a .env) stays out of the build
# context by default — no need to remember to add it here.
#
# If you add a new COPY line to the Dockerfile, add a
# matching "!" line below or the build will fail with
# "file not found".
# ============================================================

# 1. Deny everything
*

# 2. Allow back what the Dockerfile actually uses
!requirements_prod.txt
!src

# 3. Re-exclude junk that could live inside src/
src/**/__pycache__
src/**/*.pyc
src/**/*.pt
src/**/*.pth
src/**/*.safetensors
src/**/.env
src/**/.env.*